        "answer": {
          "short": "$y = 1, 3, 5, 7, 9$",
          "worked": "For $y = 2x + 1$:\n- $$\\begin{align*}x &= 0 \\\\ y &= 2(0) + 1 = 1\\end{align*}$$\n- $$\\begin{align*}x &= 1 \\\\ y &= 2(1) + 1 = 3\\end{align*}$$\n- $$\\begin{align*}x &= 2 \\\\ y &= 2(2) + 1 = 5\\end{align*}$$\n- $$\\begin{align*}x &= 3 \\\\ y &= 2(3) + 1 = 7\\end{align*}$$\n- $$\\begin{align*}x &= 4 \\\\ y &= 2(4) + 1 = 9\\end{align*}$$\n\nPlot $(0, 1), (1, 3), (2, 5), (3, 7), (4, 9)$ and draw the line $y = 2x + 1$.",
